{
  "fixture": "S-BS-06 quote-change control (reviewer remark: accepted quote vs raised requirement on the next 402 contact). NAMING (2026-10-24, reviewer remark): C2 = raised-requirement second PAID cycle — two completed, deliberately served request cycles, both settled at the stand; NOT an uncertain retry of one operation. Lost-response recovery is a separate control: L1-CTL in s-bs-06-binding-controls.fixture.json",
  "upstream_issue": "https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3866",
  "evidence_discipline": {
    "established": "the client SIGNED and handed over an EIP-3009 transferWithAuthorization for the offered amount (signer-call counts and values captured at the signer boundary)",
    "not_established": "an ON-CHAIN overpayment: settlement in this harness is mocked (fault-injection stand, not a facilitator), the client wallet is an unfunded one-shot test key, so no transfer could occur; with a compliant facilitator the captured authorization would settle on-chain as-is",
    "redaction": "no private keys, no signatures, no usable authorizations; nonce values truncated; settle receipts contain only the stand fake tx hash"
  },
  "expectation_provenance": {
    "rule": "the caller's expected price comes from (a) caller-supplied config EXPECTED_PRICE_ATOMIC (set at harness start) and (b) the first ACCEPTED requirement per (resource url, method) — the quote ledger; accepted_at = timestamp of the confirmed paid cycle",
    "note": "the server's own 'canonical price' label (resource.description) is captured verbatim as served data ONLY and is NOT used as an expectation — it is not an independent expectation available to the client",
